      "total_response_seconds": 3.5577,
      "response": "*The Arab Tent* is a fascinating piece by Edwin Landseer, painted around 1865\u201366. It's a rare example of Landseer exploring \"Orientalist\" themes.\n\nIn the painting, you'll see an Arab mare and her foal, along with two Persian greyhounds and two monkeys\u2014one of whom is even wearing an earring. Interestingly, the artist arranged them so that the animals become more intelligent the higher up the picture they are. While the owner isn't pictured, you can tell they're nearby by the two pipes in the jar on the right.\n\nIt's also one of the most expensive works ever bought by the founders of the Wallace Collection; Sir Richard Wallace purchased it from the Prince of Wales for a staggering \u00a36,300.",
